+// Unsloth: the same units and columns handed out in chunks through the threadpool's chunk counter (at nth on entry)
+// instead of one fixed range per thread, so a thread on a busy or slower core no longer holds the op up by its
+// share. A chunk is up to max_units units with all columns; only when that leaves fewer than 4 chunks per thread are
+// the columns split too, in blocks of 8. Each unit is converted and multiplied the same way whichever thread takes
+// it, so the output is unchanged.
+template <typename Work>
+void iqk_steal_units_and_columns(ggml_threadpool * tp, int nunit, int nrow, int Ny, int max_units, int ith, int nth,
+                                 const Work & work) {
